+# 01: Import new contacts from a file in our export format
+
+**What to build:** This is the first end-to-end slice of the CSV **Import** (spec: `.scratch/csv-import/spec.md`). A caller passes a CSV file as text, with the same columns as our export, to `import_contacts(repo, data)`. Every **Row** creates a new **Contact**, and the returned `ImportReport` lists the created contacts.
+
+This ticket introduces the whole public interface:
+
+- `import_contacts`;
+- the `ImportReport` dataclass, with fields `created`, `updated`, `errors` and `warnings`;
+- the `RowIssue` dataclass, with fields `row`, `column` and `message`;
+- `ImportFileError`, a subclass of `ContactError`.
+
+All four are exported from the package root. Rows are assumed valid and new here. Updates, Row errors and the remaining header rules come in later tickets.
+
+**Blocked by:** None (can start immediately)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] `import_contacts(repo, data)` accepts `str` content and returns an `ImportReport`. The four names are importable from the package root and listed in `__all__`.
+- [x] `ImportFileError` derives from `ContactError`.
+- [x] Each valid row adds a Contact to the repository. Values go through the existing validators, so the email is normalised, the name has its spacing collapsed, and the phone and tags are normalised.
+- [x] `created` lists the normalised emails in file order. `updated`, `errors` and `warnings` are empty.
+- [x] Columns are matched by header name, ignoring case and surrounding spaces, and in any order.
+- [x] The `phone` and `tags` columns are optional. If one is absent, every row is treated as having that cell blank.
+- [x] A blank phone cell means no phone.
+- [x] The tags cell is split on `;` only. Pieces are trimmed, empty pieces are dropped and repeated tags collapse, so `vip; lead;` and `vip;;lead;vip` both give `{vip, lead}`.
+- [x] An empty file is a File error (`ImportFileError`), and the repository is unchanged.
+- [x] A file containing only a header returns an empty report and imports nothing.
+- [x] A round-trip test feeds `export_csv` output straight into `import_contacts`, and the imported contacts equal the exported ones.
+- [x] Tests use only the `import_contacts` seam and check the report and the repository state, never message wording.
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `csv-import` (tip 53982c0, 83 tests passing).
