+# 02: Merge rows into existing contacts
+
+**What to build:** When an imported **Row** has the email of a **Contact** that already exists (compared case-insensitively), the row is merged into that contact instead of failing. The contact's email goes into `updated`. The merge rules follow ADR-0001: an **Import** is deliberately not the inverse of an export.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Import new contacts from a file in our export format)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] A row whose email matches an existing contact updates that contact, and its normalised email is appended to `updated` in file order.
+- [x] The row's name always replaces the stored name.
+- [x] A non-blank phone in the row replaces the stored phone. A blank phone cell leaves the stored phone unchanged.
+- [x] The row's tags are added to the stored tags, and no stored tag is removed.
+- [x] A row that changes nothing is still listed in `updated`. Every applied row appears in exactly one of `created` or `updated`.
+- [x] Importing the same file twice leaves the repository in the same state as importing it once. The second import lists every row in `updated`.
+- [x] The match against stored emails ignores case: `Ann@Example.com` in the file updates the stored `ann@example.com`.
+- [x] Tests use only the `import_contacts` seam, preload contacts with `Contact.create`, and check the report and the repository state, never message wording.
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `csv-import` (tip 53982c0, 83 tests passing).
