+# 03: Row errors, partial import and row numbering
+
+**What to build:** Invalid **Rows** are skipped and reported as **Row errors**, and the good rows are still imported (a partial import). Each issue gives the spreadsheet row number and the column, so sales can find the cell in Excel and fix the whole row in one go. This ticket also covers blank rows, and rows with fewer or more cells than the header.
+
+**Blocked by:** 01 (Import new contacts from a file in our export format)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] A blank or invalid name is a Row error on column `name`. This also applies when the row would update an existing contact.
+- [x] A blank or invalid email is a Row error on column `email`.
+- [x] A tags cell with any invalid tag is a Row error on column `tags`. A comma is not a separator, so `vip, lead` is one invalid tag and makes the row an error.
+- [x] There is one issue per bad cell. A row with a bad name *and* a bad email gives two errors.
+- [x] A row with any Row error is skipped entirely and appears in neither `created` nor `updated`. All other rows are still applied.
+- [x] `RowIssue.row` is the spreadsheet row number: the header is row 1 and the first row after it is row 2. Blank lines count in the numbering.
+- [x] A quoted cell containing a line break counts as one row, so later row numbers don't shift.
+- [x] A row is blank when it has no cells, only whitespace, or only empty cells (`,,,`). Blank rows are skipped silently, with no issue and no change to the repository.
+- [x] A row with fewer cells than the header is treated as having blank cells at the end, without a warning.
+- [x] A row with more cells than the header is processed with the extra cells ignored, plus one warning with `column=None`.
+- [x] `errors` and `warnings` are each ordered by row. Within a row they follow the header's column order, and issues with `column=None` come last.
+- [x] Tests use only the `import_contacts` seam and assert issue `row` and `column`, never message wording.
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `csv-import` (tip 53982c0, 83 tests passing).
