+# 07: Duplicate emails within one file
+
+**What to build:** When the same email appears in several **Rows** of one file (compared after normalisation, so case doesn't matter), the first row with that valid email claims it. Every later row with that email is a **Row error** that points back to the earlier row. Copy-paste duplicates in a sheet are surfaced instead of one copy silently winning. The first row keeps its claim even if it is skipped for other errors, so the duplicates are still caught after sales fixes that first row and re-imports.
+
+**Blocked by:** 03 (Row errors, partial import and row numbering)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] Two valid rows with the same email (e.g. `ann@example.com` and `Ann@Example.COM`): the first is applied, and the later one is skipped with a Row error on column `email`.
+- [x] A first row with that email that is skipped for another error (e.g. a blank name) still claims the email, so a later, otherwise valid row with the same email is a duplicate error.
+- [x] A row whose own email is invalid claims nothing.
+- [x] A third occurrence of an email is also a Row error on column `email`.
+- [x] A duplicate row's other bad cells are reported as well, one issue per bad cell.
+- [x] Tests use only the `import_contacts` seam and assert issue `row` and `column` and the repository state, never message wording.
+
+## Comments
+
+Resolved on integration branch `csv-import` (tip 53982c0, 83 tests passing).
