+# 09: Limit of 1000 contact rows
+
+**What to build:** A file may have at most 1000 contact **Rows**. A bigger file is rejected as a whole with a **File error** before any row is applied, so sales splits it instead of ending up with a half-loaded file. Every non-blank row after the header counts towards the limit, including rows that would turn out to be Row errors or duplicates. Blank rows don't count.
+
+**Blocked by:** 03 (Row errors, partial import and row numbering)
+
+**Status:** resolved
+
+- [x] A file with exactly 1000 non-blank rows after the header is imported normally.
+- [x] A file with 1001 non-blank rows is a File error (`ImportFileError`), and the repository is unchanged. No row is applied, even when the first 1000 rows are valid.
+- [x] Blank rows (empty, whitespace-only, `,,,`) don't count: 1000 contact rows plus any number of blank rows is imported normally.
+- [x] Rows that would be Row errors or duplicates do count: 999 valid rows plus 2 invalid rows is a File error.
+- [x] Tests use only the `import_contacts` seam, generate the CSV text in the test, and never check message wording.
+
