+# contactbook
+
+The core of the contacts service: the people we keep in touch with, and the ways contacts get in and out.
+
+## Language
+
+**Contact**:
+A person we keep in touch with, identified by their email address.
+_Avoid_: Lead, person, entry
+
+### Import
+
+**Import**:
+Loading a whole spreadsheet of contacts at once. A row creates a new contact or updates the existing contact with the same email.
+_Avoid_: Upload, bulk add, sync
+
+**Row**:
+One line of an imported spreadsheet, numbered the way the spreadsheet numbers it: the header is row 1 and blank lines still count.
+_Avoid_: Line, record
+
+**Row error**:
+A problem that stops a row from being imported. The row is skipped and the rest of the import goes ahead.
+
+**Row warning**:
+A problem noted on a row that was still imported, or on the header.
+
+**File error**:
+A problem with the spreadsheet as a whole that stops the import before any row is applied.
+_Avoid_: Fatal error
