@@ -0,0 +1,9 @@
+# Import merges into existing contacts instead of replacing them
+
+When an imported row matches an existing contact by email, the row is merged into the contact rather than replacing it. The name from the file always replaces the stored name. The phone is replaced only when the cell has a valid value. Tags in the file are added and never removed. So an import is deliberately *not* the inverse of an export: re-importing an edited export cannot clear a phone or remove a tag.
+
+We chose this because imports come from sales spreadsheets, not from our own export. With replace semantics, a half-filled sheet would quietly erase phones and tags we already hold. Clearing a phone or removing a tag stays a deliberate, one-contact-at-a-time action, and re-importing the same file is harmless.
+
+## Considered Options
+
+- **Replace**: the row is the contact's complete new state. It round-trips with the export, but a blank cell in a spreadsheet would destroy data without anyone noticing. Rejected.
